  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance of a wire is $R$. It is bent at the middle by $180^{\\circ}$ and both the ends are twisted together to make a shorter wire. The resistance of the new wire is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WkMI9",
      "text": "$2 R$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "owMwD",
      "text": "$R / 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "z7leR",
      "text": "$R / 4$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XRD3Y",
      "text": "$R / 8$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Resistance of wire $(R)=\\rho \\frac{l}{A}$ If wire is bent in the middle then\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nl^{\\prime}=\\frac{l}{2}, A^{\\prime}=2 A\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ New resistance, $\\mathrm{R}^{\\prime}=\\rho \\frac{l^{\\prime}}{\\mathrm{A}^{\\prime}}=\\frac{\\rho \\frac{l}{2}}{2 A}=$\r\n\r\n$\\frac{\\rho l}{4 A}=\\frac{R}{4}$",
    "image": null
  },
